/-- Balanced-quadratic Stirling target for the exact no-empty profile route.

This replaces the profile-dependent quadratic mass by the universal lower bound
`m * C(n/m, 2)`. It is stronger than the preceding Stirling target, but no longer
depends on the individual profile except through no-empty membership. -/
def PaperPartBExactNoEmptyProfileBalancedQuadraticPointwiseTarget (ε δ : ℝ) : Prop :=
  ∃ n₀ : ℕ, ∀ n : ℕ, n₀ ≤ n → InMainRange ε n →
    ∀ m ∈ Finset.range (partBPaperObstructionColorCount n + 1),
      ∀ f ∈ noEmptyColoringProfileFinset n m (partBThresholdLevel n),
        (((n : ℝ) - (m : ℝ)) * Real.log m + (m : ℝ) -
            Real.log m / 2 - Real.log (2 * Real.pi) / 2) -
          ((m * Nat.choose (n / m) 2 : ℕ) : ℝ) * Real.log 2 ≤
          partBExactNoEmptyCoarseLogCoreBudget δ n

