/-! ## Paper-backed axioms for Part B (2026-05-09)

These two axioms jointly discharge `threshold_tBoundedColoringError_le_with_error`
via the bridge chain in PartBProfileBridge.lean.

They replace the invalid `kThresholdWitness_le_n_div_threshold` axiom
(wrong direction) and provide an honest paper-backed foundation for Part B. -/

/-- Paper-backed axiom: the first-moment threshold satisfies the lower asymptotic
    `n / k_t ≥ threshold n - (1 + 2 / log 2) - η` for every fixed η > 0.

    This is the lower-bound direction of
    Heckel–Panagiotou (2023), Lemma 5 (lemma:averagecolourclass):
      n / k_t = α₀ - 1 - 2 / ln 2 + o(1)
    proved from Heckel–Riordan (2023), arXiv:2103.14014, Corollary 37 + Lemma 32
    (cited as [HRHowdoes] in HP-2023 §3.1).

    The buffer convention: B = -η < 0, so
    `partBPaperAverageClassLowerDenom B n = threshold n - (1 + 2/log 2) - B`
    is eventually positive and at most `n / k_t`. -/
axiom paperPartBThresholdAverageClassAsymptoticLowerCriterionTarget_source :
    PaperPartBThresholdAverageClassAsymptoticLowerCriterionTarget

/-- Paper-backed axiom: the scalar decay `partBExactNoEmptyDenomBinaryUniformLhs n m → -∞`
    holds uniformly for m ≤ n / partBPaperAverageClassLowerDenom B n, for any fixed B < 0.

    This is the analytic content of HP-2023 eq:wert / eq:wert2: once the average
    colour-class size is bounded below by the paper asymptotic, the quadratic +
    log-denominator LHS decays to -∞. -/
axiom paperPartBExactNoEmptyDenomBinaryLowerControlledLhsDecayTarget_source
    (B : ℝ) (hB_neg : B < 0) :
    PaperPartBExactNoEmptyDenomBinaryLowerControlledLhsDecayTarget B

